sw: LOK mixed states follow direct formatting, and colors report mixed

Patch 0003 counts a character style's attributes when a selection
spans styles. It counted them even where direct formatting covers
the whole styled span, so after setting 14 pt over text in two
styles of 12 and 18 pt the font height still read mixed, and Ely
undid the change as failed (Ely C08.2). A style's attribute now
counts only where no automatic format sets it over the span.

The font color and highlight states read the item with Get(), which
gives the default for an invalid item: a selection in red and blue
read as automatic color. Under LOK an invalid item now reports
don't-care.
